# L §2.5 (a variable over a key list takes its index from its key positions: here ks = int 1..30, from p[k]) and
# L §4.2 Keys as values ("A key of an integer index is also an int"): k <= n_max compares an int; with n_max = 12
# the lines are k = 1 and k = 12, p[k] = k.  Was LOAD-UNIT keylist and int compared.
=== m.tally
model p8
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ks = int 1..30

input n_max: int

def p[k in ks]: int = k

ask q: p[k] for k in [1, 12, 24] where k <= n_max

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n_max = 12
=== expect
q (k = 1): 1
  cut 2026-10-18
q (k = 12): 12
  cut 2026-10-18
